Chapter: XhciEventDelivery
  cites Kernel chapter Xhci
  cites Kernel chapter Pci
  grounds Device.Port, Device.Mmio

 A real command-ring event-delivery test, not a vacuous did-not-hang one.
 It discovers the controller, initialises it, sets up the event ring, rings
 the command doorbell with an ENABLE_SLOT command, then reads the event ring
 back. A working ring answers a Command Completion event (type 33) naming the
 assigned slot (1) with completion code 1 (success). A broken event-ring
 window or a CRCR cycle mismatch answers "event: NONE" instead, so this test
 fails closed if either regresses.

Section: Test
  read-event-line : Maybe Trb -> Text
  read-event-line (m) =
    when m
      is None -> "event: NONE"
      is Just (t) ->
        "event: type=" & show (xhci-event-trb-type t)
          & " slot=" & show (xhci-event-slot-id t)
          & " code=" & show (xhci-event-completion-code t)

  opening : [Console, Device.Port, Device.Mmio] Nothing = act
    let xc0 = xhci-discover
    in let xc = xhci-init-controller xc0
    in let ev = xhci-init-event-ring xc
    in let r = usb-enable-slot xc 1
    in let evt = xhci-poll-event xc 0
    in act
      print-line-uni ("found=" & (if xc0.xc-found then "1" else "0"))
      print-line-uni (read-event-line evt)
    end
  end
